CNS3D: recovery notes

cns3d.f is the program as printed in Appendix C of NASA CR-178818 (Chen 1986), the FORTRAN VII D
listing in code.pdf, one card per line. It was read from the line-printer character grid with a glyph
classifier trained on the votes of seven OCR models and checked with the original compiler, FORTRAN VII D
R05-01.00 on an emulated Perkin-Elmer OS/32, by comparing every statement's location code and every
routine's table space with the listing.

1. Cards read by inspection of the scan

Where the print is too worn for the classifier, or where checking names or running the program showed a
misreading, the card was read again from the scan; the reason is given.

  CNS3D line 4 (code.pdf page 1):  C*****[ CURVILINEAR N-S CODE FOR 3-D INCOMPRESSIBLE FLOWS ]***********
      comment as printed; worn letters (U, O, B, G) read as L, C, S, C
  CNS3D line 33 (code.pdf page 1):  1/UNSTDY/UO(21,18,10),VO(21,18,10),WO(21,18,10),DKO(21,18,10),
      COMMON /UNSTDY/ holds the previous time level: UO, VO, WO, DKO (O and 0 print alike; letter O used throughout)
  CNS3D line 34 (code.pdf page 1):  2   DEO(21,18,10),DENO(21,18,10),TMO(21,18,10)
      COMMON /UNSTDY/ second card: DEO, DENO, TMO
  CNS3D line 48 (code.pdf page 1):  C
      blank comment card; the digits are specks
  CNS3D line 55 (code.pdf page 1):  READ(5,100) NLIMT,IG,ISWP,ITT
      the D of READ is worn to C
  CNS3D line 57 (code.pdf page 1):  READ(5,200) RENL,DTT
      the card ends after DTT; the digits are specks
  CNS3D line 75 (code.pdf page 2):  PI=3.141592654
      PI as printed
  CNS3D line 76 (code.pdf page 2):  HINUM=1.E30
      HINUM=1.E30 as printed (worn U); the counterpart of SMNUM=1.E-30
  CNS3D line 110 (code.pdf page 2):  2 VISETM,DENTM
      DENTM as printed: the last two values of each restart record are read into throwaway scalars; DENIN is the inlet density
  CNS3D line 112 (code.pdf page 2):  VO(I,J,K)=V(I,J,K)
      V(I,J,K) as printed
  CNS3D line 113 (code.pdf page 2):  WO(I,J,K)=W(I,J,K)
      WO(I,J,K)=W(I,J,K) as printed
  CNS3D line 115 (code.pdf page 3):  DKO(I,J,K)=DK(I,J,K)
      DKO saves DK; CK is the wall-function constant
  CNS3D line 117 (code.pdf page 3):  DENO(I,J,K)=DEN(I,J,K)
      DENO saves the density, like UO, VO, WO
  CNS3D line 162 (code.pdf page 3):  IF(INSOU) CALL SOLVEQ(1,ISWU,ALU,SIGU,ERRU,U,UO)
      UO, the previous time level of U, as VO and WO in the next calls; O prints open like C
  CNS3D line 166 (code.pdf page 3):  IF(INSOK) CALL SOLVEQ(5,ISWK,ALK,SIGK,ERRK,DK,DKO)
      DKO, the previous time level of DK; D and O print like C and 0
  CNS3D line 173 (code.pdf page 4):  IF(ITER .GE. 20 .AND. ERRMAX .GT. 1.E03) GO TO 99
      ERRMAX as printed
  CNS3D line 193 (code.pdf page 4):  IF(ITO .GE. ITT .OR. DTT .EQ. 0.0) GO TO 999
      constant 0.0 and label 999 as printed; counter ITO
  CNS3D line 201 (code.pdf page 4):  500  FORMAT(3F8.4,3E12.4,2X,6E11.4)
      3F8.4 as printed; F3.4 cannot hold four decimals
  DIRCOS line 287 (code.pdf page 10):  IITY(III)=6
      BOTTOM wall type 6 as printed (TOP is 5, BOUNC branch 6 is BOTTOM); 6 read as 4
  TRANF line 49 (code.pdf page 11):  R3=(Z(I,J,K)+Z(I-1,J,K)+Z(I,J-1,K)+Z(I-1,J-1,K)-Z(I,J,K-1)-
      a speck made the line end in a double minus
  TRANF line 59 (code.pdf page 12):  DU(I,J,K)=PTR*(Q1*R2-Q2*R1)
      DU as printed
  TRANF line 100 (code.pdf page 12):  DU(I,J,K)=0.0
      0.0 as printed
  TRANF line 148 (code.pdf page 13):  SYW=(SY(I,J,K)+SY(I-1,J,K))*0.5
      0.5 as in the 53 neighbouring cards; a stroke through the 5 read as 0.E1
  SOLVEQ line 32 (code.pdf page 17):  PI=3.141592654
      PI as printed
  SOLVEQ line 33 (code.pdf page 17):  C-----PRESSURE CORRECTION SOLVER STARTS FROM 10
      comment as printed; worn letters (U, O, B, G) read as L, C, S, C
  SOLVEQ line 123 (code.pdf page 19):  4         DDNT*F(I,J+1,K+1)+DDNB*F(I,J+1,K-1)+
      DDNB, the north-bottom coefficient computed above (B prints like 8 and E)
  SOLVEQ line 129 (code.pdf page 19):  4         DDNT*V(I,J+1,K+1)+DDNB*V(I,J+1,K-1)+
